WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:06.695
A score threshold selects which predictions count as positive. Precision asks what fraction of that selected

00:00:06.695 --> 00:00:13.189
set is correct. Recall asks what fraction of the actual positive targets has been recovered. Their

00:00:13.189 --> 00:00:18.060
denominators describe different groups, which is why neither can replace the other.

00:00:18.567 --> 00:00:24.967
The convention includes equality. Raising the threshold changes the positive set; it does not retrain the

00:00:24.967 --> 00:00:25.367
model.

00:00:25.867 --> 00:00:30.217
There are four actual positives and two actual negatives in this tiny example.

00:00:30.733 --> 00:00:37.204
Will precision remain defined if the threshold selects no examples? Pause here and make a prediction

00:00:37.204 --> 00:00:38.013
before continuing.

00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:49.030
Precision conditions on a positive prediction. If there are no positive predictions, state the chosen empty-denominator

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:56.453
reporting convention. For our starting inputs, Threshold: 0.5. Precision: 0.75. Recall: 0.75.

00:00:56.967 --> 00:01:05.301
Recall conditions on an actual positive. Sweeping thresholds creates multiple precision-recall points; detection AP additionally needs

00:01:05.301 --> 00:01:08.427
matching and an explicit integration convention.

00:01:08.933 --> 00:01:15.477
Choose thresholds using the intended costs or a validation protocol, then report how positives are matched

00:01:15.477 --> 00:01:17.113
and metrics are aggregated.

